# Day 1 - Software Testing Fundamentals & Environment Setup

## Objective
To understand the fundamentals of software testing, learn SDLC and STLC concepts, explore testing types and levels, and set up the basic testing environment required for QA work.

---

## Tools / Setup Completed
- Installed Browsers: Chrome, Firefox, Edge
- Explored Browser Developer Tools
- Installed note-taking tool (Notion / OneNote)
- Installed screenshot and screen recording tools
- Created GitHub account and installed Git

---

## Topics Covered

### 1. Software Testing Fundamentals
- Understood the purpose of software testing
- Learned the importance of quality assurance in software development

---

### 2. SDLC Models
Studied different SDLC approaches:
- Waterfall Model
- Agile Methodology
- Scrum Framework
- DevOps Approach

Also understood where testing fits in each model.

---

### 3. STLC (Software Testing Life Cycle)
Learned STLC phases:
- Requirement Analysis
- Test Planning
- Test Case Development
- Test Environment Setup
- Test Execution
- Test Closure

---

### 4. SDLC vs STLC
Understood the difference between development and testing lifecycle and how both are connected.

---

### 5. Testing Types
Learned and classified testing types:
- Functional Testing
- Non-Functional Testing (Performance, Security, Usability)
- Maintenance Testing (Regression, Sanity)
- Change-related Testing (Re-testing, Regression)

---

### 6. Testing Levels
Learned different testing levels:
- Unit Testing
- Integration Testing
- System Testing
- Acceptance Testing

---

### 7. 7 Principles of Testing
Studied the 7 principles:
- Testing shows presence of defects
- Exhaustive testing is impossible
- Early testing
- Defect clustering
- Pesticide paradox
- Testing is context dependent
- Absence of errors fallacy

---

## Practice Activities
- Identified testing types for sample scenarios
- Mapped STLC phases with SDLC stages
- Created basic testing glossary

---

## Deliverables Completed
- Testing environment setup completed
- SDLC vs STLC comparison notes prepared
- Testing types classification notes prepared
- 7 principles examples documented
- Testing glossary created

---

## Conclusion
Day 1 helped in building a strong foundation in software testing concepts, understanding SDLC and STLC processes, and setting up the required tools for further QA practice.
